{"title": "fis", "version": "v1", "page": 37, "body": "<table>\n<thead>\n  <tr class=\"table-header\">\n    <th>Competency</th>\n    <th>Description</th>\n    <th>Examples</th>\n  </tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr class=\"row-odd\">\n    <th>Workplace</th>\n    <th>Competencies used in the workplace</th>\n    <th>General:<br>\u2022 teamwork<br>\u2022 creative thinking<br>\u2022 decision-making<br><br>IS-specific:<br>\u2022 business fundamentals<br>\u2022 problem-solving<br>\u2022 listening</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr class=\"row-even\">\n    <th>Technical</th>\n    <th>General competencies needed in a specific industry</th>\n    <th>IS-specific:<br>\u2022 IS principles and concepts<br>\u2022 IS standards and IS regulations<br>\u2022 databases management<br>\u2022 network administration<br>\u2022 risk management</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr class=\"row-odd\">\n    <th>Occupation-specific</th>\n    <th>Competencies directly related to specific positions within an industry</th>\n    <th>IS specific:<br>\u2022 cloud computing: networking, programming, machine learning, virtualization, cloud security, business concepts, and project management<br>\u2022 systems analysis: system design, data analysis, business analysis, problem-solving, critical thinking, creativity, and systems administration<br>\u2022 cybersecurity: threat detection systems, digital forensics, penetration testing, auditing, data security, data privacy</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr class=\"row-even\">\n    <th>Management</th>\n    <th>Competencies regarding leadership, conflict resolution, delegation, and team dynamics</th>\n    <th>General:<br>\u2022 team management<br>\u2022 conflict management<br>\u2022 delegation<br>\u2022 leadership<br><br>IS-specific:<br>\u2022 risk assessment<br>\u2022 policy development<br>\u2022 regulatory compliance<br>\u2022 incident response planning</th>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Table 1.1 Professional Competencies** No matter what field you go into, certain personal, academic, and workplace skills are needed to be successful as you grow in your career."}